 "posts": [
  {
   "slug": "home-office-deduction-explained",
   "title": "The home office deduction, explained in five minutes",
   "date": "2026-10-22T08:00:00",
   "categories": [
    "tax"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "deductions",
    "freelancers"
   ],
   "featured_media": "home-office",
   "excerpt": "If you work from home for yourself, part of your rent and bills may be deductible. Here is who qualifies and how to calculate it.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>If you are self-employed and work from home, a share of your housing costs may be deductible. The rules are stricter than many people think, but for those who qualify, the saving is real.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who qualifies</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"ticks\"} --><ul class=\"wp-block-list ticks\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>The space is used <strong>regularly and only</strong> for work. A kitchen table does not count.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>It is your main place of business, or where you meet clients.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>You are self-employed. Most employees cannot claim it.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Two ways to calculate it</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"is-style-left\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-table is-style-left\"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>How it works</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Simplified</td><td>A fixed rate per square foot, up to a limit</td><td>Small spaces, little paperwork</td></tr><tr><td>Actual expenses</td><td>A share of rent, utilities and insurance by floor area</td><td>Larger spaces, higher costs</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><!-- /wp:table -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"tip-box\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group tip-box\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p><strong>Tip:</strong> measure the room and take a photo of it set up for work. If you are ever asked, that is your best evidence.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Not sure which method gives the bigger deduction? We run both for every freelance client and use the better one.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "sticky": true,
   "format": "standard",
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Priyanka S.",
     "email": "priya@example.com",
     "content": "The simplified method saved me hours this year. Thanks for the clear table.",
     "date": "2026-10-23T10:15:00"
    },
